<!DOCTYPE html> 
<html lang="en"> 
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Web Programming FAQ</title></head> 
<body> 
<section id="faq"> 
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2> 
 
  <details open> 
    <summary>What is a hyperlink?</summary> 
    <p>A hyperlink is a clickable link that takes users to another 
       webpage, file, or location within a page.</p> 
  </details> 
 
  <details> 
    <summary>What is an HTML element?</summary> 
    <p>An HTML element is a part of a webpage created using tags, 
       such as headings, paragraphs, images, and links.</p> 
  </details> 
 
  <details> 
    <summary>What is a CSS selector?</summary> 
    <p>A CSS selector is used to choose which HTML elements should 
       receive a particular style.</p> 
  </details> 
 
  <details> 
    <summary>What is responsive web design?</summary> 
    <p>Responsive web design makes websites adjust their layout 
       to work well on different screen sizes and devices.</p> 
  </details> 
</section> 
</body> 
</html>
